          "prompt": "# In app.py, add near the bottom, inside the `if \"posts\" in st.session_state:` block:\nfrom save_posts import save_posts\n\nif st.button(\"Save approved posts\"):\n    edited_posts = {\n        post_type: st.session_state[f\"edit_{post_type}\"]\n        for post_type in st.session_state[\"posts\"]\n    }\n    paths = save_posts(edited_posts)\n    st.success(f\"Saved {len(paths)} post(s):\")\n    for path in paths:\n        st.code(path)",
          "verify": "In the running Streamlit app, edit at least one post's text, then click \"Save approved posts\". Open the newly saved file for that post type and confirm it contains YOUR edited text, not the AI's original draft.",
